<span id="S3.T6.2.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">No, there’s clear evidence that the MMR (measles, mumps, rubella) vaccine does not cause autism. | vaccines (but not MMR), caused autism. | More recently, some parents have been concerned that too many vaccines given too soon might cause autism. (<a href="https://www.babycenter.com/404_does-the-mmr-vaccine-put-my-child-at-greater-risk-for-autism_11518.bc" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://www.babycenter.com/404_does-the-mmr-vaccine-put-my-child-at-greater-risk-for-autism_11518.bc</a>)</span>
