<span id="S3.T6.2.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">cause autism. | Brian Hooker PhD, linking vaccines as a plausible cause of autism. | in the cause of autism Dr. (<a href="http://vaccinationdecisions.net/vaccines-and-autism/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">http://vaccinationdecisions.net/vaccines-and-autism/</a>)</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T6.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T6.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td>
<td id="S3.T6.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S3.T6.2.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:42.7pt;">
<span id="S3.T6.2.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">25.301</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S3.T6.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S3.T6.2.5.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:341.4pt;">
<span id="S3.T6.2.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">The belief that vaccines cause autism is not just wrong, but damaging. | Also, the component in vaccines that is "causing autism," hasn’t been in vaccines since the 90s. | Furthermore, if you believe that vaccines cause autism, the only way a vaccine could cause autism is if the disease that the child is being vaccinated (<a href="http://www.debate.org/opinions/are-vaccines-causing-autism" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">http://www.debate.org/opinions/are-vaccines-causing-autism</a>)</span>
</span></td></tr>
