<span id="S3.T6.2.8.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:42.7pt;">
<span id="S3.T6.2.8.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">22.865</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S3.T6.2.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S3.T6.2.8.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:341.4pt;">
<span id="S3.T6.2.8.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">May 13, 2008 WASHINGTON (AP) — Parents claiming that childhood vaccines cause autism should not be rewarded by the courts when the scientific community | Court of Claims alleging that vaccines caused autism and other neurological problems in their children. | Lawyers for the families are presenting three different theories of how vaccines caused autism. (<a href="http://www.infowars.com/families-make-case-for-vaccine-link-to-autism/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">http://www.infowars.com/families-make-case-for-vaccine-link-to-autism/</a>)</span>
</span></td></tr>
