<td id="S3.T6.2.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb">
<span id="S3.T6.2.10.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:42.7pt;">
<span id="S3.T6.2.10.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">22.719</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S3.T6.2.10.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb">
<span id="S3.T6.2.10.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:341.4pt;">
<span id="S3.T6.2.10.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">The special "vaccine court" ruled yesterday, in three separate cases, each of which was testing a different strategy for claiming that vaccines cause autism | , that there was no evidence that vaccines caused autism in any of the cases. | The judges rule against the notion that MMR vaccine causes autism, and against the notion that thimerosal used as a preservative in vaccines causes autism (<a href="http://genome.fieldofscience.com/2009/02/special-court-rules-that-vaccines-are.html" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">http://genome.fieldofscience.com/2009/02/special-court-rules-that-vaccines-are.html</a>)</span>
</span></td></tr>
